course: dictionary
lesson: 2031
title: Confiture: the French word for jam
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Confiture is a French word. In French it means jam, the sweet spread made from fruit and sugar that you put on bread. «Confiture de fraises» means strawberry jam.
explain: Say it like «kon-fee-TOOR», with the stress on the last part. In French it is feminine, so it goes with la: la confiture means "the jam".
explain: In English, confiture is rare and fancy. You might see it on a posh jar or a menu, but most English speakers say jam, jelly or preserves instead.
fact: Confiture means jam, or fruit preserve, in French.
fact: «Confiture de fraises» means strawberry jam, and «confiture d'abricots» means apricot jam.
fact: «Du pain, du beurre et de la confiture» means bread, butter and jam.
fact: In English, people usually say jam (UK), or jelly or preserves (US).
fact: Confiture is a noun, and it is feminine: la confiture.
exercise: In French, what does «confiture» mean? | Milk | *Jam | Butter | Bread
exercise: «Confiture de fraises» means which kind of jam? | *Strawberry jam | Honey | Apricot jam | Orange juice
exercise: Copy the French word for jam from «du pain, du beurre et de la confiture». | beurre | pain | *confiture | et
test: Which French phrase means apricot jam? | la peinture | *confiture d'abricots | du pain | confiture de fraises
test: Why might a posh jar in England say «confiture»? | *Because it is a rare, fancy word for jam | Because it means bread in English | Because it is a type of cheese | Because it means a car
exam: Which article goes with confiture, as in «___ confiture»? | *la | une | un | des
